\subsection{L2 high-resolution scan: the LDS W-structure}
\label{sec:l2_w}

To precisely locate the LDS feature, we performed a dense scan of 201 points over the interval $s\in[0,1]$ on the L2 Sierpi\'{n}ski gasket ($N=15$, 27 edges). The enhanced diagnosis reveals a double-valley structure, which we designate the \textbf{LDS W-structure} (Fig.~\ref{fig:l2_w}).

The primary valley is at $s=0.275$ with depth $0.1111$, a relative drop of $30.3\%$ from the left shoulder ($0.1593$ at $s=0.10$). A secondary valley appears at $s\approx0.550$ with depth $0.136$. Between the two valleys, at $s=0.400$, there is a central peak of $0.1574$.

The default diagnosis shows no corresponding extrema at either valley position; it exhibits a smooth U-shaped background ranging from $0.0687$ to $0.1552$. The structural contrast between the W-shaped enhanced diagnosis and the featureless default diagnosis constitutes the strongest evidence for Silent Discordance in the fractal-graph system.

