\subsection{Draho\v{s}'s independent replication and control experiments}

Rastislav Draho\v{s} replicated the fractal W-structure with independent code. He also identified and fixed a coding issue ($XX+ZZ$ instead of $XX+YY+ZZ$); the W-structure persisted after the fix. Control experiments on comparable graphs gave: ring graph depth $0.071$ at $s=1.00$; random graph depth $0.048$ at $s=2.00$; tree graph, no valley at comparable scan resolution\footnote{The tree-graph result was obtained at low scan resolution. A subsequent high-resolution study (to be reported separately) reveals a weak valley; this does not affect the present conclusions about the fractal graph.}. The primary LDS valley depth ($0.1111$) is approximately $1.6$ times the ring and $2.3$ times the random graph.

\subsection{Local-probe analysis}

Draho\v{s} divided edges into local (near the defect) and bulk (distant). The local valley depth rose with increasing $\chi$, while the bulk contribution was diluted. The W-structure is a localized defect mode.

\subsection{Tensor-RG toolchain}

Draho\v{s} built a tensor-RG toolchain to test thermodynamic-limit survival~\cite{Drahos2026GitHub}. The energy RG is exact through L2. Draho\v{s}'s impurity-explicit RG reproduces the L2 local valley depth of $0.1902$ to the digit, confirming the W-structure as a localized defect mode. The L3 depth does not converge on available hardware---across the truncation dimension it wanders ($\approx0.24/0.08/0.20$). This is a real convergence limit, not a model defect. The full toolchain is publicly available.

\subsection{Contradiction-edge position}

Changing the contradiction edge from $(0,2)$ to $(0,1)$ completely eliminated the W-structure. The injection point is decisive.

\subsection{TAT blind test}

Sultanov's TAT ensemble analysis tested 13 metrics. TAT gave only boundary anchors and was silent at the valley positions, confirming the W-structure as a smooth modulation.

\section{Cycle enhancement: an empirical condition}

The control experiments support an empirical condition we call \emph{cycle enhancement}. Cycles are not strictly necessary, but they enhance stability, depth, and robustness. The fractal graph has the deepest valley structure; the ring and random graphs have shallower valleys; the tree graph shows no valley at low resolution. We refrain from calling this a ``law'' because no analytical mechanism is yet established.

\section{Mechanism: a tentative picture}

The contradiction edge injects tension into the relational field. When injection is asymmetric---the two subgraphs separated by the edge are not equivalent---the field undergoes a sudden, localized reorganization of its correlation structure, appearing as a W-structure in the enhanced diagnosis. The self-similar nature of the Sierpi\'{n}ski gasket may underlie the emergence of two valleys at different scales. When injection is symmetric, tension is absorbed uniformly and no valley appears. This picture is consistent with the decisive effect of edge position, the enhancement by cycles, and the blindness of the default diagnosis. We present it only as a guide for future work, not as an established mechanism.

\section{Limitations}

\begin{enumerate}
\item All cross-graph scans except the fractal graph were at $N=6$.
\item All experiments were performed on three separate personal computers, one for each of the three authors, located in different countries.
\item All diagnostics were on the ground state.
\item The high-resolution scan was performed only for L2; L1 and L3 were scanned at lower resolution.
\item The L1 valley is weak (relative depth $3\%$) and may be affected by finite-size effects.
\item Valley depths carry a systematic uncertainty of $6\%$--$20\%$.
\item Strong evidence is currently confined to the fractal graph. L3 ($N=42$) tensor-RG scaling was attempted but did not converge on available hardware (valley depth wanders across truncation dimensions); the question remains open.
\item The thermodynamic-limit behavior remains unresolved; a tensor-RG toolchain is available~\cite{Drahos2026GitHub}.
\end{enumerate}

\section{Conclusion}

We discovered Silent Discordance in the PXP model and provided strong evidence in a self-built fractal-graph quantum system. High-resolution scanning reveals a W-shaped double-valley structure in the enhanced diagnosis, which we designate the Li-Draho\v{s}-Sultanov W-structure. The primary valley has depth $0.1111$ ($30.3\%$ relative to the left shoulder), has been independently replicated, and is enhanced by cycles. The PXP-model signal is confirmed to be distinct from quantum many-body scar-state crossing by a direct half-chain entanglement entropy calculation. The discovery was made under strict methodological constraints. The thermodynamic-limit question remains open and is explicitly scoped.

